      "dom_id": "step-q12329",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14223637/assets/aee38b4fa46a403ee9517fc5a087434c8205b6553a4ebefa43be74ba7babfbc0.png)\n\nUsing the graphical method, find the solutions $(x,y)$ of the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=x+1 \\\\ y={x}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The solutions $(x,y)$ of the system correspond to the intersection points of the two curves.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14223637/assets/563850386ee40e291a04911a2216614bda567ffbb8cfce1a7713400900d2701c.png)\n\nFrom the graph, the curves intersect at \n\n$\\,$ $(0,1)\\,$ and $\\,(1,2).$ \n\nTherefore, these are the solutions of the corresponding system.",
