      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14223637/assets/e1892e632e2485b17400ba9d2a9372bf164e20812c3b6fe4f9b03ab1348fab7d.png)\n\nUsing the graphical method, find the solutions $(x,y)$ of the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=f(x) \\\\ y=g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The solutions $(x,y)$ of the system correspond to the intersection points of the two curves.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14223637/assets/8dfab4aa640e596227bd6a6a09af36264f6bce9bc0906a69ea433d6e6a3db78d.png)\n\nFrom the graph, the curves intersect at \n\n$\\,$ $(-1,1)\\,$ and $\\,(2,1).$ \n\nTherefore, these are the solutions of the corresponding system.",
