      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14223637/assets/e6831eff5d8feb87ebba8e7d449d98fbe72c3ed4df01d8374d4866e8e3456ddc.png)\n\nUsing the graphical method, find the solutions $(x,y)$ of the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=-x+1 \\\\ y={x}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The solutions $(x,y)$ of the system correspond to the intersection points of the two curves.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14223637/assets/e1ebbb0ce147dc986dd4d47539f055407c9b870af2ada9629520c4fa1d9aef33.png)\n\nFrom the graph, the curves intersect at \n\n$\\,$ $(-2,3)\\,$ and $\\,(1,0).$ \n\nTherefore, these are the solutions of the corresponding system.",
